course: dictionary
lesson: 2726
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One small word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Read the words around «dip» and ask what is happening. In «She dipped her biscuit in her tea», she put the biscuit into the liquid for a moment.
explain: The same word can mean a drop. In «The road has a dip just before the bridge», the clues are road and bridge, so a dip is a low place. In «The temperatures dipped overnight», the numbers went down a little.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. The meaning "put into liquid" does not fit «The sun dipped below the horizon», so that is a different sense. When a word has many meanings, the topic of the sentence is your best clue.
fact: Dip can be a verb (to dip) or a noun (a dip).
fact: To dip means to put something into a liquid quickly and take it out, as in «dip your toe in».
fact: To dip also means to go down a little, as in «temperatures dipped».
fact: A dip can be a thick sauce, like salsa or hummus, or a quick swim.
exercise: «She dipped her biscuit in her tea.» What does dipped mean? | A thick sauce to eat | A quick swim in the sea | Went down a little, like a road | *Put into a liquid quickly and taken out
exercise: «The road has a dip just before the bridge.» What is a dip here? | A thick sauce you eat with crisps | A quick swim in a lake | *A low place in the road | A month with 31 days
exercise: In the knuckle trick, «months that land in a dip have fewer» days. What is a dip in this trick? | *A gap between two knuckles, where the months have fewer days | A bag for shopping | A knuckle with a ring on it | A gap between two knuckles
test: «Temperatures dipped overnight.» What does dipped mean? | *Fell a little | Turned into ice | Stayed exactly the same | Went up sharply
test: Yuki says, «I'm going for a dip in the lake.» What is a dip here? | *A quick swim | A bag for shopping | A kind of dance | A hard test
exam: «Ella dipped her chips in the hummus.» What does dipped mean? | Ran away | Went down a little, like a road | *Put quickly into a food and taken out | Fell asleep
